Z||000000||DaveL||04-30-2001||08:32 AM||||I know this must have been discussed to death, but I must ask one more time. Haven't had much luck with a search.<P>I have access to a bunch of used instrument clusters, for about $50 I can get a nice looking one. I found a local shop that buys old Fieros and puts the Lamborgini kits on them. My question is are they interchangeable, and will the guages still work? My 87 SE 2.5 has the 80 mph speedo, while most of the clusters in this guys place are 120 mph. The connectors look the same.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||04-30-2001||08:47 AM||||I'm pretty sure the speedo is plug'n'play.  You may need to re-calibrate the tach to work with your 4 cyl since the 120 clusters were in v-6 cars only.  I don't believe this is a problem though.<P>The cluster that has the 120 speedo more than likely accompanied the ralley gage cluster mounted over the radio.  Your cluster probably has the oil pressure gauge (or maybe a volt meter if it is an 84) under the tach.  I think the 120 cluster does not have a gauge under the tach.  The oil pressure gauge is in the ralley cluster along with a volt meter.<P>Maybe you're planning on only changing out the speedometer (guess I should re-read your post more closely).  The older gauges were reflective lit while the newer (including the 120 speedo cluster) are backlit and are much brighter.<P>Theogre's cave might have some info (see the link at the bottom of this page).   Also try this link for some good info:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html</A> <P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||04-30-2001||02:09 PM||||Correct, they are plug and play.  Change the entire cluster so you can get the brighter lights.  I did this on my kit car.<P>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaveL||04-30-2001||03:51 PM||||I have read some posts that talk about doing something to the tach, there seems to be some confusion about this, at least on my part. If they are totally plug and play, I'm getting one!||||reg||5
